Track 1: Lens Cap Scratches the Parapet
- Story & Context: On a freezing October night on a Thames River warehouse roof, Silas dropped his heirloom telescope eyepiece into the gravel just as Iron-Sight laid down the hook for their first master tape. The ambient crunch of broken glass accidentally caught on the room mic was pitched down and layered over a pulverizing 85 BPM breakbeat, capturing the night the crew traded street-corner freestyle battles for heavy, amplified grieving. The track captures the exact moment their meteor-wound guitar rig blew out a tube, creating the genre's signature distorted siren hum. Connecting to their origin, the original metallic scrapings from the broken scope were fed directly through the clockwork spring-reverb box to create the song's haunting intro. "We counted satellite flashes just to prove the sky was still listening to the basement."
