Track 2: The Apogee of Corvo Street
- Story & Context: This track centers on Corvo Street's notorious fence, a former maritime engineer known as "Deep-Tide" Vance, who secretly traded stolen nautical gear for imported East Coast vinyl. Iron-Sight writes from the perspective of a young courier running packages through icy alleyways while struggling with the sudden overdose of his older brother. The music drops into a bare, weeping electric guitar motif—its notes dragging like heavy clock gears—before a thunderous hardcore rap verse cuts through the sorrow. The chorus fuses a sample of ticking brass gears with a crushing wall of fuzz guitar, marking the character's descent into cold survival mode. "He traded his father’s pocket watch for twenty yards of copper wire and a clean kick drum."
