Track 3: "Is That Cassiopeia Bleeding?"
- Story & Context: Local myth says this track was recorded in a single take during a blackout caused by a coastal storm, illuminated only by lantern light and glowing amp tubes. DJ K-Ration scratched a spoken-word weather broadcast over a slow, crushing drop-D guitar riff while Iron-Sight delivered a surreal, exhausted eulogy for their abandoned neighborhood. The title came from a faded chalk drawing left on the roof by a departed crew member, pointing toward the northern sky. The song fades out on a two-minute ambient tail of winding clockwork mechanisms fading slowly into pure, hum-laden electric guitar feedback. "Leave the amplifier hum running after we drop the mic into the harbor."
